# starling-quantize recipe: Granite-Speech-4.1-2B, phone (1472 MB): every
# linear Q4_K (8x8 i8mm repack on arm64), as granite-q40-h4.recipe otherwise.
# enc.input_linear (160 wide) falls back to Q8_0.
#
# Measured (2026-10-12, FLEURS test, 100 clips per language, paired bootstrap
# vs all-Q8_0): en 6.22 % vs 6.18 % (clip +0.11 pt [-0.45, +0.76]), de 5.82 %
# vs 5.78 % (-0.28 pt [-1.03, +0.37]). On a 30-clip German BF16 spot check it
# sat closer to BF16 than the Q4_0 file. Matrix and gate:
# docs/quantization.md, "Phone recipes".
#
#   build/starling-quantize --input models/granite-speech-4.1-2b-bf16-exact.gguf \
#       --output models/granite-speech-4.1-2b-q4k-h4.gguf \
#       --recipe quants/recipes/granite-q4k-h4.recipe \
#       --imatrix models/granite-calib160.imx --f32-1d
default q4_k
^llm\.embed\.weight$ q4_k
conv_(up|down)\.weight$ q4_k
